## ABSTRACT

The Food Integrity Scanner is a proposed five-modality portable instrument combining Near-Infrared (NIR) spectroscopy, Surface-Enhanced Raman Spectroscopy (SERS), Differential Pulse Voltammetry (DPV), an Electronic Tongue (ET) potentiometric/voltammetric array, and a CRISPR-Cas12a microfluidic cartridge — unified by a cloud-based multi-modal AI fusion engine and anchored to a blockchain trust layer. This document establishes the complete mathematical, architectural, and technical specification foundation for the FIS platform. Every claim is grounded in peer-reviewed literature published between 2022 and 2026.

