### 1.6 Multi-Modal Sensor Fusion Mathematics

Given NIR spectral vector x_NIR ∈ ℝᵖ¹, Raman vector x_Raman ∈ ℝᵖ², Electronic Tongue response vector x_ET ∈ ℝᵖ³, and CRISPR fluorescence probability scalar γ ∈ [0,1]:

**Low-level (early) fusion — direct concatenation:**
x_fused = [x_NIR | x_Raman | x_ET | γ] ∈ ℝᵖ¹⁺ᵖ²⁺ᵖ³⁺¹

**Mid-level fusion — latent variable concatenation:**
x_mid = [T_NIR | T_Raman | T_ET] ∈ ℝˢ¹⁺ˢ²⁺ˢ³

**Late (decision-level) fusion — weighted posterior combination:**
P_final(c) = Σⱼ wⱼ · Pⱼ(c | modⱼ), Σⱼ wⱼ = 1

Methods commonly applied in conjunction with multi-block regression include sequential and orthogonal partial least squares regression (SO-PLS), parallel and orthogonal partial least squares regression (PO-PLS), and canonical correlation analysis. SO-PLS is suitable when there is a pattern or order associated with the data blocks, while PO-PLS is used when equal importance is assigned to each data block. [NCBI](https://ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9875022) These are the state-of-the-art mathematical frameworks for heterogeneous multi-modal food data fusion.

